Whatever, loser.

750
00:53:55,580 --> 00:53:57,420
But I'll make it quick if that's what you
want.

751
00:53:57,500 --> 00:53:57,500
Enough!

752
00:53:57,600 --> 00:53:58,600
Both of you!

753
00:53:58,624 --> 00:53:59,624
Good grief.

754
00:54:00,030 --> 00:54:02,439
Shinobi hand-to-hand
combat is a traditional

755
00:54:02,440 --> 00:54:05,020
drill passed down from
generation to generation.

756
00:54:05,344 --> 00:54:07,924
You might think it's
stuffy to be so formal, but

757
00:54:07,925 --> 00:54:10,400
here at the academy we
have respect for tradition.

758
00:54:10,644 --> 00:54:11,700
This stuff matters!

759
00:54:12,745 --> 00:54:14,685
First you always face
and make this one-handed

760
00:54:14,686 --> 00:54:16,881
sign toward your
opponent before starting.

761
00:54:16,954 --> 00:54:19,579
It represents half of the
two hands used to activate

762
00:54:19,580 --> 00:54:21,921
a jutsu and indicates
your intention to fight.

763
00:54:22,584 --> 00:54:24,640
Now we call this the spar sign.

764
00:54:25,905 --> 00:54:29,880
When you finish sparring and the bout is
concluded, you each extend forth the

765
00:54:29,881 --> 00:54:33,660
unison sign and lock your fingers around
each other's.

766
00:54:33,669 --> 00:54:36,660
This indicates that you recognize each
other as comrades.

767
00:54:37,294 --> 00:54:40,100
That's the etiquette of Shinobi
hand-to-hand combat.

768
00:54:41,500 --> 00:54:42,880
Are you listening, Naruto?

769
